<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amda Seyon I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">acceded <a href="/years/1314">1314</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Amda Seyon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amda Seyon I was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> who acceded in 1314. He conducted successful campaigns against the Muslim states to the east and south, greatly expanding the power and territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty">Solomonic dynasty</a>. His reign is regarded as a key stage in the foundation and military consolidation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amda-seyon-i.jpg" alt="Amda Seyon I" width="303" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amda_Seyon1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
